From c93e992bca52d20bee3e1416f66ab90619169ce9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sacha Gavino <sacha.gavino@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 22:04:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stage 4 Part 1a: precompute grain-rank / phase / ice index
 maps

set_dependant_rates and get_temporal_derivatives recovered a grain bin rank on
every RHS call by slicing species names and re-parsing them with
read(c_i,'(I2)') -- a formatted internal read run thousands of times per step --
and by re-classifying each surface species with a chain of string comparisons.
All of that is a pure function of the species/reaction list, so it is now
precomputed once at init.

build_index_maps() (called after read_reactions) fills four lookups:
  SPECIES_GRAIN_RANK(nb_species)     grain rank from species_name(i)(2:3), J/K
  SPECIES_PHASE(nb_species)          1 = surface (J), 2 = mantle (K), 0 = other
  SPECIES_ICE_CODE(nb_species)       0 none / 1 CO / 2 H2O / 3 NH3 / 4 CO2 /
                                     5 CH4 / 6 CH3OH, mirroring the (4:11) tests
  REACTION_C4_GRAIN_RANK(nb_reactions) rank of product slot 4, for the ER/CIR
                                     accretion corrections

The five hot-loop sites (rate_tot accumulation in get_temporal_derivatives; the
hoping-rate loop; the ab_tot/ab_surf/ab_mant + ice-abundance loop; the three
Eley-Rideal / complex-induced blocks; the surface/mantle sum in the 3-phase
routine) now read these maps. Iteration order and every arithmetic operation are
unchanged, so the RHS is bit-identical; only the per-call name parsing is gone.
All 15 read(c_i,'(I2)') calls in ode_solver.f90 are removed.

This is Part 1a of two: the IMOD1/IMOD2 tunnelling/modify classification is a
separate commit (its base-then-modify control flow is isolated on purpose so a
later bisect can localise it).

Verified byte-identical against the pre-change build on four configurations:
the tabulated reference case; a derived 4-bin MRN case (abundances.out,
elemental_abundances.out and dust_distribution.out); and an is_er_cir=1 run that
exercises the ER/CIR blocks (site 4), which the default is_er_cir=0 cases never
reach. tests/roundtrip_derived.sh still passes byte-identical.
